    {
      "id": "claim_e11753bbf3054a72a2db438f851d702e",
      "statement": "The Pi package ships an npm shrinkwrap that npm installs verbatim without filtering optional dependencies by os and cpu, so esbuild's binary for all twenty-six platforms lands in the tree — 285 MB of a 610 MB layer — with exactly one usable.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/prune-platform-packages.js#L5-L11",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cefeeaedb2b797e18fd67ce30d0bdd161d25fd9823853f1b8bdf1a2ab51654f8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0e20f47140394a50b618d8f2eae9a7c2",
      "statement": "The prune script keeps the shrinkwrap and prunes afterwards by npm's own rule, because deleting the shrinkwrap would re-resolve every transitive dependency to a fresh caret range on each build and trade reproducibility for size.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/prune-platform-packages.js#L9-L11",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bdd1f8ed891e840206e7ef66cafc6c36aaa1b3281a394676c008b40109638024:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5effb48438ba4d23ac551a4a8658f90a",
      "statement": "The script reimplements npm's os/cpu constraint rule: absent or empty means no constraint, entries may be negated with a leading !, and a package is removed when either field excludes the running platform or architecture.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/prune-platform-packages.js#L31-L44",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:89c12176a6a0466f4f56df53e2e6efbc09feaeae09987a0a076347f64ef9555e:"
